    "id": "1COVER-faq-official-policy-clai-29",
    "content": "### What Destination Do I Choose for my cruise?\n\nFirstly, you’ll need to make sure you select the [Cruise Add-On](https://www.1cover.com.au/cruise-travel-insurance/), so you’re covered for things like emergency medical assistance, emergency medical and hospital expenses on board the cruise, cancellation fees, lost deposits, and more.\n\nYou must select the countries that your cruise is travelling to, so you can ensure that you are covered within that region. This includes all stops your cruise will be making, even if you do not plan to leave the ship. Please refer to our [Cruise Region list here](https://www.1cover.com.au/faqs/cruise/regions/). When applying for a policy, you must select the region appropriate to the countries the ship will visit.\n\nTravellers on domestic cruises in Australian waters should select the Australia Cruise region.\n\n\n[<< Back to FAQs Home](https://www.1cover.com.au/faqs/)\n\n#### Need Further Assistance?\n\n[Message Us](https://www.1cover.com.au/contact/form/)\n\n[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/1Cover/)\n\nAll FAQ answers are based on the current effective [PDS](https://www.1cover.com.au/policydetails/). If your policy is older than the current PDS, please contact us or refer to your particular policy.\n\nAny information contained on this website is general advice only and has been prepared without taking into account your objectives, financial situation or needs. You should consider these having regard to the [PDS](https://www.1cover.com.au/policydetails/).\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.1cover.com.au/faqs/cruise/what-destination-do-i-choose/](https://www.1cover.com.au/faqs/cruise/what-destination-do-i-choose/)",
