    "content": "### Does Apia Home and Contents Insurance cover Flood?\n\nApia Home and Contents Insurance covers loss or damage caused by flood1. 'Flood' means the covering of normally dry land by water that has escaped or been released from the normal confines of a lake, a river, a creek etc.\n\nApia Home and Contents Insurance does not cover loss or damage caused by storm surge unless the loss or damage occurs at the same time as the insured loss or damage to your home and/or contents caused by storm\\*.\n\n[Learn more about Home & Contents Insurance](https://www.apia.com.au/home-insurance/home-and-contents.html)\n\n\n\\*Actions or movements of the sea are not covered. For full details of the covers, limitations, exclusions and conditions and what constitutes a 'flood' please read the Apia Home and Contents Insurance Product Disclosure Statement.\n\nAustralian Pensioners Insurance Agency Pty Limited ABN 14 099 650 996 is an authorised representative of AAI Limited ABN 48 005 297 807, the product issuer. Please read the Apia Home and Contents Insurance Product Disclosure Statement before making any decision regarding this product. Call us on 13 50 50 for a copy. This advice has been prepared without taking into account your particular objectives, financial situations or needs, so you should consider whether it is appropriate for you before acting on it.\n\n1There is no cover for flood in the first 72 hours of your policy. Very limited exceptions apply. Read the [PDS](https://www.apia.com.au/policy-documents.html#home-contents) for more detail.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.apia.com.au/faqs/home-contents/does-apia-home-and-contents-insurance-cover-flood.html](https://www.apia.com.au/faqs/home-contents/does-apia-home-and-contents-insurance-cover-flood.html)",
