    "id": "BINGLE-faq-official-policy-clai-27",
    "content": "### Does Bingle cover me if I hire a car overseas? — Does Bingle offer any optional extras?\n\nYes, Bingle has several optional extras on offer. You have the option to select these when you take up [Comprehensive Car Insurance](https://www.bingle.com.au/comprehensive-car-insurance) - you can add them when you get a quote or add them later in self-service to an existing policy. We offer [Windscreen and Glass cover](https://www.bingle.com.au/comprehensive-car-insurance/windscreen-cover) which means if you have this option and need to make a claim we'll replace your broken windscreen, sunroof or windows without you having to pay an excess. We also have [Keep Mobile cover](https://www.bingle.com.au/comprehensive-car-insurance/hire-car) which provides you with a hire car in the event of an incident. Is your car 3 years old or less? You can choose to take up [New for Old](https://www.bingle.com.au/comprehensive-car-insurance/new-for-old) which means if your car is determined by us to be a write-off we will replace it with a brand new car of the same make and model (where available).\n\nOptional extras benefits are subject to the terms, conditions, limits, and exclusions of the insurance policy. You can't add optional extras after an incident and have damage or loss covered for that same incident. Optional extras must be added to your policy before the incident you're claiming for. Please refer to the ++[PDS](https://www.bingle.com.au/policy-documents)++ for more information.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs](https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs)",
