    "id": "BINGLE-faq-official-policy-clai-51",
    "content": "### Does car insurance cover broken windows?\n\nYour windscreen and window glass is considered part of 'your car' which means it is covered under your comprehensive car insurance policy, however your standard excess applies.\n\nThat's why we created our Windscreen and Window Glass Only cover. It gives you protection for times when the only loss or damage to your car is to the windscreen or window glass and you won't have to pay an excess.\n\nSay your windscreen is cracked after a passing truck flicked up rocks. If you have this optional extra1 on your policy, you can relax knowing you have car insurance to cover your broken windscreen and no excess to pay.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs](https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs)",
