    "id": "BINGLE-faq-official-policy-clai-8",
    "content": "### If I am in an accident that is not my fault do I still have to pay an excess?\n\nWe'll usually ask that you pay the excess when you first make your claim. We'll waive the excess if you or the driver didn't contribute to the accident (this means the other driver was entirely at fault). You'll need to provide us with the name and address of the person who was at fault, and the registration number of the vehicle(s) involved.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs](https://www.bingle.com.au/faqs)",
