    "id": "COVER_MORE-faq-official-policy-clai-15",
    "content": "### Will Cover-More Travel Insurance cover me if I am travelling with expensive luggage?\n\nMost of our travel insurance plans include [luggage and travel documents cover](https://www.covermore.com.au/travel-insurance/benefits/luggage-insurance), which can protect items such as your phone, camera, laptop, jewellery, watch or one item specified by you.\n\nThe benefit limit per plan can be seen below, however, item limits do apply.\n\n| Plan | Maximum Benefit Limit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Maximum Benefit Limit | $25,000 |\n| International Comprehensive | $15,000 |\n| International Basic | $5,000 |\n| Inbound Plan | $15,000 |\n| Domestic Comprehensive+ | $15,000 |\n| Domestic Comprehensive | $5,000 |\n| Domestic Basic | $Nil |\n\nPlease refer to the [Product Disclosure Statement](https://www.covermore.com.au/pds) (PDS) for coverage limits.\n\nIf you’re travelling with expensive luggage, you may be able to increase your luggage item limit for an additional cost when you apply for a quote. The extra cover can then be added to your policy for an additional premium.\n\nIf you make a luggage claims, receipts or valuations no more than 24 months old must be available if requested by our team.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.covermore.com.au/frequently-asked-questions](https://www.covermore.com.au/frequently-asked-questions)",
