    "id": "FAST_COVER-faq-official-policy-clai-188",
    "content": "### Can I buy Snow cover just for the time that I am skiing?\n\nSnow Sports cover isn’t usually available just for part of your trip, as the Snow Sports Plus policy normally applies to your whole journey.\n\nHowever, you may be able to purchase a separate Snow Sports Plus Already Overseas policy just for the days you’ll be participating in snow sports listed in our PDS. In this case, the snow sports and snow-related benefits will only apply for the dates shown on your Certificate of Insurance under your Snow Sports Plus Already Overseas policy.\n\nIt’s important to know that an Already Overseas policy can only be purchased once you’re already travelling and has some key differences compared to policies starting in Australia: it comes with a $500 excess, a 48-hour waiting period before cover begins, an age limit of 65 years, and it can only be issued for a maximum of 21 days.\n\nFor more information on your policy options, give our Aussie-based customer service team a call on 1300 409 322. We’re available Monday to Saturday, 9am–5pm AEST.\n\nEligibility criteria, policy terms, conditions, exclusions, limits and sub-limits apply. The information provided is general advice only and does not take into account your personal objectives, financial situation or needs. Please read the PDS before deciding if a policy is right for you.\n\n#### Related Articles\n\n- What is Snow Sports cover?\n- What type of policy is the Snow Sports Plus policy?\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://fastcover.com.au/faq/can-i-buy-snow-cover-just-for-the-time-that-i-am-skiing](https://fastcover.com.au/faq/can-i-buy-snow-cover-just-for-the-time-that-i-am-skiing)",
