    "id": "RACQ-faq-official-policy-clai-43",
    "content": "### Which travel insurance policy do I select if I am going on a cruise?\n\nCover is provided for river cruising and ocean cruising regardless of whether you are cruising overseas or within Australia. A number of options are available subject to the terms, conditions and exclusions in the policy.5\n\nThe definition of Cruise means an ocean voyage on a commercially operated vessel for more than one night. If you are on a cruise for only one night or you are on a river cruise, you will automatically be covered under the policy without selecting the Cruise Option.\n\nThe policy cannot cover any medical expenses within Australia, so if your cruise might be in Australian waters, please check carefully if there are medical facilities onboard, and if so, whether Medicare applies.\n\n5Refer to [Combined Product Disclosure Statement (PDS) / Financial Services Guide (FSG)](https://www.racq.com.au/insurance/insurance-disclosure-documents#travel) to determine if Cruise Cover is required for your trip. Terms, conditions, limits, sub-limits and exclusions apply.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.racq.com.au/help-contact/insurance/which-policy-do-i-select-if-i-am-going-on-a-cruise](https://www.racq.com.au/help-contact/insurance/which-policy-do-i-select-if-i-am-going-on-a-cruise)",
