    "id": "SHANNONS-faq-official-policy-clai-26",
    "content": "### Shannons Home and Contents Insurance covers a wide range of insured events. Some of the things it can include are:\n\n* Cover for loss of, or damage to, your home and/or contents from insured events like fire, storm, theft --- plus flood cover included as standard on your Home \\& Contents policy.\n* Enthusiast Items cover automatically included when you insure your contents --- protecting up to $10,000 of automotive tools, memorabilia and collectables, the things that matter most to a motoring enthusiast.\n* \"New for old\" replacement regardless of age --- Shannons will rebuild or replace your home, contents or enthusiast items new for old (or pay the assessed cost of doing so), up to your sum insured or the applicable limit.\n* Legal liability cover included as standard, helping protect you if someone is injured or their property is damaged at your insured address, and you're found liable.\n\nYou can also add Optional Accidental Loss or Damage cover and Optional Personal Effects cover (for items you take out of the home, like laptops, phones and sunglasses) for an extra premium.\n\nThe full cover includes much more, so it's important to read the Product Disclosure Statement \\[PI16.1\\]for a complete list of inclusions, limits and exclusions.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.bingle.com.au/graphql/execute.json/aeminsuranceeds/FAQListSortable;tag=insurance](https://www.bingle.com.au/graphql/execute.json/aeminsuranceeds/FAQListSortable;tag=insurance)",
