    "id": "SHANNONS-faq-official-policy-clai-13",
    "content": "### Is temporary accommodation covered?\n\nIt depends. Your temporary accommodation benefit covers reasonable and necessary costs if your home is unsafe and can't be lived in.\n\nIt's important to check your [policy documents](/policy-documents \"\") to understand your temporary accommodation benefit.\n\nThese documents, along with your Certificate of Insurance, explain your benefit limit and if any exclusions apply.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://www.bingle.com.au/graphql/execute.json/aeminsuranceeds/FAQListSortable;tag=insurance](https://www.bingle.com.au/graphql/execute.json/aeminsuranceeds/FAQListSortable;tag=insurance)",
