    "id": "SCTI-faq-official-policy-clai-10",
    "content": "### What do I need to provide if I'm claiming for medical expenses?\n\nIf you need to make a claim for medical expenses, here are some documents that we may require when assessing your claim: Receipts for your medical expenses, together with any consultation notes or reports provided by the treating doctor. If your claim is related to costs to see a medical specialist, please send us your referral letter. This is the letter your GP would have sent to the specialist. If you have been admitted to hospital or have incurred ambulance costs, please send us a full admission and discharge summary, or any other reports the hospital gave you. Please keep a copy of your documents and receipts for your own records. We may ask for them during your claims assessment Sometimes we may need to obtain information not described above, and we will notify you if this is the case. If you don’t provide the information required, it may result in a delay with the processing of your claim.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://scti.com.au/faqs](https://scti.com.au/faqs)",
