    "id": "SCTI-faq-official-policy-clai-2",
    "content": "### What happens once I've submitted my claim?\n\nOnce you submit a claim, we will send you an email to acknowledge we received it. This email will also let you know how long it will be before we aim to have a claims assessor contact you. We need you to complete the Declaration and Privacy Act form. A link to the form will be included in your email. Although you’ve already provided authority to us, the majority of third parties will require this form prior to releasing information to us. Completing the form and sending it to us immediately can reduce any delays. If we require further information from you and/or a third party (such as your doctor, travel agent or the police),your claims assessor will keep you updated with the progress and about what information is required. When we have made a decision about your claim, your claim assessor will confirm the outcome to you. We’ll always confirm the decision in writing, but may call you to discuss it first.\n\n*Canonical Source:* [https://scti.com.au/faqs](https://scti.com.au/faqs)",
